From: Lewis Gibson <12851394+lewisgibson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:03:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reapply the position of an entity that is teleported to
 another region

Entity#transform, which positions the copy of an entity that teleportAsync
carries across a region border, only called setPosRaw. snapTo, which the same
region teleport and vanilla use, also calls reapplyPosition, which runs the
setPos overrides. Entities whose block position, bounding box or culling box
is derived in setPos were therefore left at their old block: an item frame, a
glow item frame, a painting or a leash knot kept the BlockAttachedEntity#pos
of the region it left, so its bounding box and its support check pointed at a
block that region owns, survives() failed and the entity was discarded; the
position it then saved as block_pos was rejected as too far from the entity
on the next hop. A display entity kept the culling box of its old position.

The invariant: an entity that has been transformed for a teleport is in the
state setPos would have given it at the destination, exactly as after snapTo.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index 75dabd3e7b6077b5ae8ee30048786442742b93f9..85a235bf727d7bda38b88a022a048c5e8d714f52 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -4425,6 +4425,7 @@ public abstract class Entity
         }
         if (pos != null) {
             this.setPosRaw(pos.x, pos.y, pos.z);
+            this.reapplyPosition(); // Folia - region threading - snapTo does this, and entities derive their block position and bounding box from setPos, see BlockAttachedEntity#setPos
         }
         this.setOldPosAndRot();
     }
